    "duration_raw": "1 hour/level (D) or until discharged",
    "saving_throw_raw": null,
    "spell_resistance_raw": null,
    "description_raw": "Choose a single touch range spell of 4th level or lower with a casting time of 1 standard action or less. As part of the action of casting spite, you cast the associated spell and bind it into a defensive ward in the form of a tattoo, birthmark, or wart somewhere upon your body. The next time you are hit by a melee attack or a combat maneuver is used successfully against you, the stored spell is triggered against your foe. You do not need to succeed on a touch attack to affect the target, but in all other respects the spell is treated as though you had cast it normally. If the attacking creature is not a valid target for the spell, the stored spell is lost with no effect.\n\nYou can have only one spite spell in effect at a time; if you cast this spell a second time, the previous spell effect ends.",
